<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia's SIMPAR reports 1996 profits.</title>
<headline>Tunisia's SIMPAR reports 1996 profits.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisian real estate firm Societe Immobiliere et de Participation (SIMPAR) made a 664,000 dinar net profit in 1996, results showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>No comparative figures were available for 1995.</p>
<p>Turnover was 5.915 million dinars in 1996, and operating profit 688,000 dinars. Total balance sheet was 107.688 million dinars.</p>
<p>The company was listed in January 1997 on the Tunis Stock Exchange after it sold a 30 percent stake of its capital to the public as part of the government's privatisation programme.</p>
<p>Its share was last priced 25.56 dinars on the bourse.</p>
<p>($1=1.08 dinar)</p>
</text>
